      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The concerns about debt and inflation are entirely valid arguments from those who oppose the Green New Deal, as the proposed spending is enormous. However, the economic models supporting the plan argue that the long-term costs of climate inaction—disaster relief, agricultural failure, and public health crises—will dwarf the cost of the transition. Furthermore, government investment in green tech will actually *reorganize* supply chains toward sustainable, resilient domestic production, rather than simply destabilizing them.",
      "source": "target",
