    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. It sounds like you're saying the long-term benefits basically justify any immediate financial or structural damage. So, if we're being realistic, isn't the most effective economic path just a gradual, market-driven transition instead of this massive government-led overhaul? It seems like the 'radical reform' approach is inherently more risky for the economy.",
